    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What this workflow does\n\n1. The webhook receives an uploaded document and company ID.\n2. A small deterministic node checks request fields and filename.\n3. FastAPI /route extracts PDF text or runs vision OCR for photos/scans and records route metadata.\n4. FastAPI runs Extractor, Validator and RAG-grounded Coder; each stage appends an audit event to traces.db.\n5. n8n branches to Accept or Exception Handler → Escalate, then returns the decision.\n\nInspect stored values in the DocDesk Document Ledger; export the current ledger as CSV for Excel.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 620
      },
      "id": "5f0c1a52-6a7e-4b8f-9d31-0c2e7a4b1008",
      "name": "Architecture Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        200,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Why each component exists\n\n- n8n is the visible workflow coordinator: it passes data between steps and chooses the accept/escalate/fail branch.\n- FastAPI does document OCR, agent calls, RAG retrieval, validation, and SQLite writes.\n- The Validator uses Python checks first (amount arithmetic, required tax ID, duplicate marker); LLM explanation is conditional.\n- RAG returns company-specific rules to the Coder, which must cite a retrieved rule.\n- Each stage output and skill version is inspectable in the API trace and DocDesk ledger.\n- Human corrections are appended to the audit history; they do not overwrite the original extraction.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 620
      },
      "id": "5f0c1a52-6a7e-4b8f-9d31-0c2e7a4b1009",
      "name": "Design Decisions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        860,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyMinute"
            }
          ]
        },
        "simple": false,
        "filters": {
          "q": "label:docdesk has:attachment {filename:pdf filename:png filename:jpg filename:jpeg filename:webp}"
        },
        "options": {
          "downloadAttachments": true,
          "dataPropertyAttachmentsPrefixName": "attachment_"
        }
      },
      "id": "docdesk-gmail-·-invoice-attachments",
      "name": "Gmail · Invoice Attachments",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmailTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
      "position": [
        180,
        820
      ],
      "disabled": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "const out = [];\nconst allowed = new Set([\"pdf\", \"png\", \"jpg\", \"jpeg\", \"webp\"]);\nfor (let i = 0; i < $input.all().length; i++) {\n  const item = $input.all()[i];\n  for (const [key, meta] of Object.entries(item.binary || {})) {\n    const filename = meta.fileName || key;\n    const ext = filename.split(\".\").pop().toLowerCase();\n    if (!allowed.has(ext)) continue;\n    const buffer = await this.helpers.getBinaryDataBuffer(i, key);\n    const clean = String(item.json.id || Date.now()).replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9_-]/g, \"\");\n    out.push({json: {body: {doc_id: `email-${clean}-${key}`, company_id: \"company_b\", filename, file_b64: buffer.toString(\"base64\"), source: \"email\"}}});\n  }\n}\nreturn out;"
      },
      "id": "docdesk-normalize-email-attachments",
      "name": "Normalize Email Attachments",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        440,
        820
      ]
    },
